  "conventions": {
    "clock": "Unix epoch milliseconds in UTC. Numeric fields shown as strings for epochs, sequences and revision counters in WS examples, unless explicitly numeric.",
    "interpolation": "Replace ${...} transport credentials only in the test environment. Each example request or message is a complete application payload. WebSocket handshake framing headers are supplied by the standard client. No private key, reusable token or active endpoint is included.",
    "proof": "Raw 32-byte Ed25519 public key, 64-byte signature and proofInput use unpadded base64url. publicKeyHash is sha256:<lowercase hex> over the raw public key. proofInput decodes to the UTF-8 canonical JSON challenge. Use the exact decoded bytes when signing or verifying. The connector checks audience, purpose, request, key, binding and expiry. The verifier uses its stored single-use challenge, validates the signature, checks server time and consumes it once.",
    "digest": "GA-01 v1 uses RFC 8785 JSON Canonicalization Scheme (JCS) and SHA-256 over its UTF-8 bytes, formatted sha256:<lowercase hex>. digestVectors contains the exact input objects. The fixture checker covers these vectors with ASCII property names, ordinary JSON scalars (including 23.5) and unchanged array order. These vectors cover only a subset of JCS.",
    "credentials": "Tenant write examples use the target same-origin user session and CSRF token. Device requests use their enrollment or connection credential only. No credentials in URL query strings, event bodies or evidence logs.",
    "phases": "Each case is an independent branch of the successful scenario. http and websocket list complete wire examples. timeline gives their order; local evidence is fixture metadata, not a wire message."
  },
